  target-surface
    role action
    defined-by output
    precondition "A composed translation is proposed as a complete surface in its target language."
    effect "Reject output containing a response label, a translation arrow or an unexpanded template delimiter using the shared structural fragments; do not certify incomplete composition."
    unit "boolean completeness verdict"
    example "A surface containing an unexpanded double-bracket template remains incomplete."
    grounding "js/worker/formal_ai_worker_translation_composition.js::targetTranslationSurfaceComplete; js/agentic/crate/formalization_grammar.mjs::structuralRuleValues"
  numeric-identity
    role action
    defined-by quantity
    defined-by same
    precondition "A formalized numeral is assigned an identity or read back during translation."
    effect "Use the shared resolved prefix only for a verified numeric value; preserve the exact surface under the unresolved prefix when the numeric interpretation is uncertain."
    unit "typed numeral identity"
    example "English 987,65 retains its original surface under the unresolved prefix rather than claiming the value 98765."
    grounding "js/agentic/crate/formalization_grammar.mjs::numericIdentityPrefix; rust/src/formalization/mod.rs::numeric_identity_prefix"
  answer-compatibility
    role action
    defined-by answer
    precondition "A typed question and answer are compared, but at least one typed evidence record is absent."
    effect "Return unknown with the shared missing-evidence reason; absence of typed evidence establishes neither compatibility nor contradiction."
    unit "compatibility status and reason"
    example "A missing question or answer produces unknown with reason missing typed evidence."
    grounding "js/agentic/crate/dialogue_formalization.mjs::answerCompatibility; rust/src/formalization/dialogue.rs::answer_compatibility"
  proposition-structure
    role action
    defined-by output
    precondition "A formalized statement carries connectives, quantifiers, an explicit count or comparison relations that a set of term identities cannot hold."
    effect "Read the ordered proposition shape, the ordered relations and the explicit repetition from the seeded vocabulary and add them to the statement identity; structure the reader cannot bind stays an unresolved obligation instead of a guess."
    unit "proposition shape, relations, repetition and unresolved obligations"
    example "1 and 2 and 1 or 2 receive different shapes, and print hello twice keeps a repetition that print hello lacks."
    grounding "js/agentic/crate/proposition_structure.mjs::readPropositionStructure; rust/src/formalization/proposition_structure.rs::read_proposition_structure"
  comparison-relation
    role action
    defined-by output
    precondition "A comparison word such as less than, greater than or at most joins two operands of a statement."
    effect "Map the word to an ordered relation and its direction, swapping the operands of a converse word so a paraphrase and its original share one relation while reversed operands stay distinct."
    unit "ordered relation over two operands"
    example "2 is greater than 1 and 1 is less than 2 both read less(1,2); 2 is less than 1 reads less(2,1)."
    grounding "js/agentic/crate/proposition_structure.mjs::relationOf; rust/src/formalization/proposition_structure.rs::relation_of"
  output-repetition
    role action
    defined-by output
    precondition "A program request binds a quoted output and states how many times it is printed: an explicit count right after the output, or a later mention marked as a repetition."
    effect "Bind the output once per counted or explicitly repeated mention, in request order; every other mention of the same literal is the same output obligation, so the program never prints a line the request did not ask for twice."
    unit "ordered output lines of one program"
    example "prints Hello twice and prints Hello and then prints Hello again bind two lines; print exactly Hello and code prints Hello exactly bind one."
    grounding "js/agentic/crate/intent_formalization_obligations.mjs::boundOutputLiterals; rust/src/intent_formalization/obligations.rs::bound_output_literals"
  task-decomposition
    role action
    defined-by output
    precondition "A request names more than one obligation joined by a sequence, alternative or aggregation connective of the seeded vocabulary."
    effect "Split the request into a task tree within the seeded depth, breadth and budget bounds, derive a test per task, draft by cache, derivation and composition, select the passing draft of least action and compose the children by their relation; a task no draft passes stays an explicit unresolved result."
    unit "task tree with tests, drafts, selection and composition"
    example "Translate hello to French, then count the letters and report the vowels reads sequence(leaf,aggregation(leaf,leaf)) in English, Russian, Hindi and Chinese alike."
    grounding "js/agentic/crate/meta_executor.mjs::executeProcedure; rust/src/meta_executor.rs::execute_procedure"
  symbolic-operator
    role action
    defined-by output
    precondition "A statement writes a relation or arithmetic operator as a symbol between two operands."
    effect "Read the symbol as the same relation its words name, keep operand order for non-commutative operators, sort the operands of commutative ones, and leave a chain of different operators unresolved because its grouping is not read."
    unit "ordered relation over two operands"
    example "a - b reads minus(a,b) and b - a reads minus(b,a); 1 < 2 reads less(1,2) like 1 is less than 2."
    grounding "js/agentic/crate/proposition_structure.mjs::operatorSymbols; rust/src/formalization/proposition_structure.rs::operator_symbols"
  typed-statement-notation
    role action
    defined-by output
    precondition "A formalized statement has typed dialogue evidence alongside its legacy term identities."
    effect "Render both legacy terms and escaped typed meaning through the shared statement template, preserving negation and substituting each original slot once; retain legacy notation alone when no typed meaning exists."
    unit "Links Notation statement"
    example "A quantity statement retains its currency in typed meaning as well as its original term identities."
    grounding "js/agentic/crate/page_formalization.mjs::statementNotation; rust/src/formalization/page.rs::statement_notation; rust/src/seed.rs::fill_template_once"
